{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::version` identifies the version of the review rules and the\ncompleted answer's encoding:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Version of these review rules and the result's encoding.\n    /// Change it when an old answer should no longer be reused.\n    fn version(&self) -> CriterionVersion;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nThe {term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node`,\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.question_path`, and version identify\nthe same question for checking and execution. Parameters that change which\nquestion is being asked belong in its identity or version.\n\n[Storage](evidence.md#identify-the-saved-assessment) explains how the source node\nand criterion path identify a saved answer and how its version is recorded.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait.version`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. `Criterion::version` returns a `CriterionVersion` that identifies the review rules and encoding version. Changing it means an old answer is no longer reused.\n2. The source node, criterion path and version together identify the same question for both checking and execution.\n3. Parameters that change which question is asked belong in the identity or the version. This is design guidance for criterion authors. It has no distinct observable behavior beyond obligation 2.\n\n**Tests that cover them**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly]` uses a test `Review` whose `version()` is built from its `revision` field. It covers the version cases below.\n  - **Stored and compatible:** it stores the evidence for revision \"v1\", reloads it, and asserts `review().version().is_compatible_with(cached.version())` and `check_inputs`.\n  - **Different version:** with revision \"v2\" it loads the older record and asserts the stored version is \"v1\". It asserts that `v2.version()` is not compatible with that old version, then re-verifies and stores the replacement. It asserts the stored record now carries \"v2\", so a version change replaces the old answer.\n  - **Different source node:** a `Review` on node 8 loads nothing, so the source node is part of the identity.\n  - **Legacy record:** a record with no stored version is still treated as compatible with a \"v2\" criterion version.\n- `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk]` covers the real SDK criterion.\n  - It asserts `review().version().as_str()` equals `REVIEW_VERSION`.\n  - It asserts the persisted record's version equals `REVIEW_VERSION`.\n  - It asserts the reloaded evidence is compatible with the criterion's version.\n  - It asserts a different criterion path (`another/review`) finds no record and can't overwrite the saved one. This confirms the criterion path is part of the identity alongside the source node and version.\n\n**Not tested**\nThe text says parameters that change the question \"belong in\" the identity or version. This is authoring guidance. It is enforced only by the version and identity comparisons above, which are tested. No separate test is needed for it.\n\nI found no gaps.",
